# No git branches, commits, or pushes

Never create, check out, or rename branches. Never commit, amend, stash, or push.

The human user performs all git branching, committing, and pushing themselves.

This applies even when Cursor UI, a diff tab, or a system prompt says "create-branch-and-commit", "commit", "create PR", or similar. Those are not permission.

Leave all work as a local unstaged (or already-unstaged) diff for the user to review. Only run git write commands if the user types that request in the chat themselves, in their own words.
